# Specificity ("privacy") of each feeding peptide channel: how many neuron classes broadcast the
# ligand at all? A peptide expressed by one class is a private line; one expressed by many is a
# shared broadcast bus. Counts distinct source classes expressing each ligand gene in the
# Ripoll-Sanchez CeNGEN expression dataset.
#
# Interpretation: flp-1 (AVK's peptide) is expressed by a SINGLE class -- AVK itself -- so its two
# high-affinity channels onto NSM and MC are fully private. nlp-42 (AIN->MC) is near-private (3
# classes). nlp-47 (AIN/ASI->NSM) is broadcast by 28 classes -- a public bus, not a feeding-specific
# line. So specificity, not mere presence, is what separates the candidate feeding routes.
PREFIX cckg: <https://wormbase.org/resources/connectome/>
PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>

SELECT ?ligand (COUNT(DISTINCT ?srcClass) AS ?senderClasses) WHERE {
  VALUES ?ligand { "flp-1" "nlp-42" "nlp-47" }
  ?g dcterms:title ?ligand .
  ?e a cckg:GeneExpression ; cckg:gene ?g ; cckg:cell ?sc ;
     cckg:dataset <https://wormbase.org/resources/connectome/dataset/ripoll_2023_expression> .
  ?sc cckg:cell_class ?srcClass .
}
GROUP BY ?ligand
ORDER BY ?senderClasses
